      "message": "We allow setting TX and RX on the same instance. Although in reality you should not apply a SA to both directions, in tests you can do that (e.g. we do that in IpSecManagerTest).\n\nPreviously I was thinking that if someone takes CTS as examples of using APIs, they may be confused by seeing a IpSecTransformState has both TX and RX. But it\u0027s probably fine because those setters are for tests. In tests, setting TX and RX on the same instance are valid use cases.",
